1. Overview & Key Concepts

Incident: An unplanned interruption to an IT service or a reduction in the quality of an IT service (e.g., system outage, application crash, printer malfunction).

Objective: Restore normal service operation as quickly as possible and minimize business impact.
2. Incident Lifecycle

[ Identification & Logging ] ──► [ Categorization & Prioritization ] ──► [ Investigation & Diagnosis ] ──► [ Resolution & Closure ]


3. Key Process Steps

Step 1: Identification & Logging

Incidents are logged automatically (via monitoring/email) or manually by the Service Desk/User via the portal.

Mandatory fields must be completed: Caller, Short Description, Category, and Subcategory.
Step 2: Categorization & Prioritization

Impact: Measures the effect of the incident on business operations (High, Medium, Low).

Urgency: Measures how quickly the incident requires resolution (High, Medium, Low).

Priority Matrix: Calculated automatically based on Impact and Urgency:
