Step 3: Investigation & Diagnosis

Assign the incident to the appropriate Assignment Group and Assigned To individual.

Move state to In Progress.

Document diagnostic steps in Work Notes.

If waiting on user information, vendor action, or a dependent change, set state to On Hold with an appropriate On Hold Reason.

Step 4: Resolution & Closure

Once service is restored, select an appropriate Resolution Code (e.g., Solved (Permanently), Solved (Workaround)) and enter Resolution Notes.

Change state to Resolved.

The incident will automatically close (Closed) after the defined auto-closure period if no further action is taken by the requester.

4. Fulfiller Quick Checklist

[ ] Verify caller and contact information.

[ ] Ensure correct Category and Subcategory are set.

[ ] Validate Priority calculation (Impact vs. Urgency).

[ ] Keep state up to date (In Progress, On Hold, Resolved).

[ ] Provide clear, customer-friendly resolution details upon completion.
